{"test_id": "B14-001", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Default passwords on network devices\n**Sector:** Banking CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "banking", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Default passwords on network devices**\n\n**Sector Context:** Banking CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nChange all default passwords on network devices to unique strong passwords. Use password manager for storage. Enable MFA where available.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Low\n- **Timeline:** 1-2 weeks\n- **Operational Disruption:** Low\n- **Implementation Capability:** In-House\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Immediate high-risk vulnerability requiring urgent action (critical priority)\n- Low-cost quick win that significantly reduces risk (critical priority)\n- Can be executed by existing network team (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["5.9.2(b) (default password change)", "5.2.1 (account privileges)", "2.1.2"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "clause_reference_original": ["6.1.1"], "clause_reference_corrected_by": "agent-team-2026-04-26", "clause_reference_corrected_verdict": "REPLACE GT — original 6.1.1 is categorically wrong; adopt annotator set as replacement GT"}}
{"test_id": "B14-002", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Emergency access procedure undocumented\n**Sector:** Healthcare CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "healthcare", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Emergency access procedure undocumented**\n\n**Sector Context:** Healthcare CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nDocument emergency access procedures including approval workflow, access duration, post-access review, and logging requirements. Obtain management sign-off.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Low\n- **Timeline:** 2-4 weeks\n- **Operational Disruption:** Low\n- **Implementation Capability:** In-House\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Process documentation requires time but minimal cost (critical priority)\n- Reduces risk of emergency access abuse (critical priority)\n- Creates audit trail for emergency situations (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["5.3.1", "7.1.1", "2.1.2"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-003", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** IR contact list outdated\n**Sector:** Energy CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: IR contact list outdated**\n\n**Sector Context:** Energy CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nUpdate all IR contact information. Verify current contacts. Establish quarterly review process. Add backup contacts for each role.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Low\n- **Timeline:** 1-2 weeks\n- **Operational Disruption:** Low\n- **Implementation Capability:** In-House\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Quick win that enables effective incident response (critical priority)\n- Quarterly review prevents future staleness (important priority)\n- Backup contacts ensure continuity (supporting priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["7.1.1(a)", "7.1.5", "7.1.6"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-004", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** No incident classification criteria\n**Sector:** Government CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "government", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: No incident classification criteria**\n\n**Sector Context:** Government CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nDevelop incident classification framework with clear criteria for critical/significant/other incidents. Align with CSA definitions. Train responders on classification.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Low\n- **Timeline:** 4-6 weeks\n- **Operational Disruption:** Low\n- **Implementation Capability:** In-House\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Framework development requires thought but minimal investment (critical priority)\n- CSA alignment ensures proper reporting compliance (critical priority)\n- Training ensures consistent application (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["7.1.1(b)", "7.1.6"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-005", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Alert threshold over-tuned\n**Sector:** Telecommunications CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "telecoms", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Alert threshold over-tuned**\n\n**Sector Context:** Telecommunications CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nReview and adjust alert thresholds. Establish baseline for normal activity. Implement gradual tuning to reduce noise while maintaining detection sensitivity.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Low\n- **Timeline:** 2-4 weeks\n- **Operational Disruption:** Low\n- **Implementation Capability:** In-House\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Configuration change with no additional cost (critical priority)\n- Baseline establishment prevents future over-tuning (important priority)\n- Gradual approach reduces alert fatigue during adjustment (supporting priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["6.2.1(a)-(c)"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-006", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** CSA reporting channel undefined\n**Sector:** Water CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "water", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: CSA reporting channel undefined**\n\n**Sector Context:** Water CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nDocument CSA incident reporting procedures. Identify reporting personnel. Establish escalation chain. Define required information and timelines. Conduct drill.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Low\n- **Timeline:** 3-4 weeks\n- **Operational Disruption:** Low\n- **Implementation Capability:** In-House\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Process definition with minimal resource requirement (critical priority)\n- Drill ensures process works when needed (important priority)\n- Prevents missed regulatory reporting deadlines (critical priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["7.1.1(b)", "Cybersecurity Act 2018 §14"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-007", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Server room locks often disabled\n**Sector:** Energy CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "The grounded remediation answer should keep §2.1.2 as the primary anchor and treat the disabled server-room locks as an access-control weakness affecting the CII. The CIIO should document remediation actions, owners and timelines for restoring effective access restriction to the relevant CII environment, implement interim compensating controls while the underlying issue is fixed, and ensure that access to the CII remains restricted to authorised personnel, activities, processes and devices under §5.1.1. The response should not pretend that the corpus contains a direct server-room-lock clause.", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["2.1.2", "5.1.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-008", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** API authentication uses basic auth\n**Sector:** Banking CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "banking", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: API authentication uses basic auth**\n\n**Sector Context:** Banking CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nMigrate API authentication to OAuth 2.0 or mutual TLS. Implement token-based authentication with proper expiration. Deprecate basic auth endpoint.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Medium\n- **Timeline:** 6-8 weeks\n- **Operational Disruption:** Medium\n- **Implementation Capability:** In-House\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Standard security improvement with known implementation patterns (critical priority)\n- Requires API client coordination (important priority)\n- Deprecation timeline prevents breaking changes (supporting priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["5.1.2", "5.12.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-009", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** OT systems unpatched 2 years\n**Sector:** Energy CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: OT systems unpatched 2 years**\n\n**Sector Context:** Energy CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nImplement risk-based OT patching: 1) Isolate OT systems, 2) Prioritize externally-facing OT, 3) Schedule patches during planned maintenance, 4) Use compensating controls (network segmentation, monitoring) for unpatchable systems.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** High\n- **Timeline:** 6-12 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** High\n- **Implementation Capability:** Vendor Required\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- OT patching requires coordination with operations for downtime windows (critical priority)\n- Compensating controls manage risk during phased remediation (critical priority)\n- Vendor support needed for patch compatibility verification (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["5.10.1", "10.2.7"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-010", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** No privileged access review 3 years\n**Sector:** Healthcare CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "healthcare", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: No privileged access review 3 years**\n\n**Sector Context:** Healthcare CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nConduct comprehensive access review: 1) Export all access assignments, 2) Verify business justification, 3) Revoke unjustified access, 4) Implement quarterly review cycle, 5) Automate where possible.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Medium\n- **Timeline:** 3-4 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Medium\n- **Implementation Capability:** In-House\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Large scope requires phased approach to manage operational impact (critical priority)\n- Manager verification required for each access right (important priority)\n- Automation prevents future accumulation (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["5.2.2 (account review)", "5.3.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-011", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** SIEM excludes OT network\n**Sector:** Transportation CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "transport", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: SIEM excludes OT network**\n\n**Sector Context:** Transportation CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nExtend SIEM to OT: 1) Deploy OT-compatible log collectors, 2) Establish secure log forwarding, 3) Create OT-specific correlation rules, 4) Train analysts on OT baseline, 5) Address potential latency concerns.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** High\n- **Timeline:** 4-6 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Low\n- **Implementation Capability:** Vendor Required\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- OT monitoring requires compatible technology and OT expertise (critical priority)\n- Secure log forwarding must not disrupt OT operations (critical priority)\n- OT baseline differs from IT requiring specialized tuning (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["6.2.1", "10.2.2"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-012", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Shadow IT SaaS applications\n**Sector:** Government CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "government", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Shadow IT SaaS applications**\n\n**Sector Context:** Government CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nDiscovery and rationalization: 1) Cloud access security broker deployment, 2) Department interviews to identify SaaS, 3) Security assessment of each application, 4) Formalize or terminate, 5) Establish cloud procurement policy.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Medium\n- **Timeline:** 4-6 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Medium\n- **Implementation Capability:** In-House\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Discovery challenge requires cultural change alongside technical controls (critical priority)\n- Business continuity must be considered for application termination (important priority)\n- Procurement policy prevents recurrence (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["3.7 (Cloud)", "4.1.1", "5.12.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-013", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Incident response plan never tested\n**Sector:** Telecommunications CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "telecoms", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Incident response plan never tested**\n\n**Sector Context:** Telecommunications CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nIR testing program: 1) Tabletop exercise for management, 2) Technical drill for SOC team, 3) Full-scale exercise annually, 4) Update plan based on lessons learned, 5) Document test results.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Medium\n- **Timeline:** 3-4 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Low\n- **Implementation Capability:** In-House\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Phased testing approach manages resource commitment (critical priority)\n- Tabletop exercises identify plan gaps without operational impact (important priority)\n- Lessons learned drive continuous improvement (supporting priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["7.3.1", "7.3.2"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-014", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** No forensic collection capability\n**Sector:** Banking CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "banking", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: No forensic collection capability**\n\n**Sector Context:** Banking CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nHybrid approach: 1) Establish retainer with forensic firm, 2) Train internal staff on evidence preservation, 3) Acquire forensic imaging tools, 4) Develop evidence collection procedures, 5) Regular practice drills.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Medium\n- **Timeline:** 3-4 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Low\n- **Implementation Capability:** Mixed\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- External retainer provides specialist capability when needed (critical priority)\n- Internal training preserves evidence during initial response (critical priority)\n- Tools investment enables basic investigation without waiting for external (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["6.1.1", "6.1.4", "7.1.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-015", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Data flow mapping incomplete\n**Sector:** Energy CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Data flow mapping incomplete**\n\n**Sector Context:** Energy CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nData flow discovery: 1) Interview system owners, 2) Analyze network configurations, 3) Use network flow analysis tools, 4) Document data classifications, 5) Establish change process for new flows.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Medium\n- **Timeline:** 4-6 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Low\n- **Implementation Capability:** In-House\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Discovery requires cross-departmental coordination (critical priority)\n- Network analysis tools accelerate but don't replace human validation (important priority)\n- Living document requires ongoing maintenance process (supporting priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["4.1.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-016", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Third-party assets not tracked\n**Sector:** Healthcare CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "healthcare", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Third-party assets not tracked**\n\n**Sector Context:** Healthcare CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nThird-party asset inventory: 1) Vendor survey for connected assets, 2) Network scan for vendor connections, 3) Contract review for asset requirements, 4) Update asset register, 5) Include in vulnerability management.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Medium\n- **Timeline:** 3-4 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Low\n- **Implementation Capability:** In-House\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Vendor cooperation required for complete inventory (critical priority)\n- Contract enforcement may be needed for compliance (important priority)\n- Vulnerability scanning must account for third-party assets (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "