{"test_id": "B14-017", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** IT/OT convergence unmanaged\n**Sector:** Water CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "water", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: IT/OT convergence unmanaged**\n\n**Sector Context:** Water CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nArchitecture review and controls: 1) Map all IT/OT connections, 2) Security architecture review, 3) Implement DMZ between IT and OT, 4) Establish change management for new connections, 5) Monitor cross-boundary traffic.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** High\n- **Timeline:** 6-9 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Medium\n- **Implementation Capability:** Consultant Required\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Architecture review requires specialized IT/OT security expertise (critical priority)\n- DMZ implementation provides controlled boundary without operational disruption (critical priority)\n- Change management prevents future unmanaged convergence (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["10.2.1", "10.2.3"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-018", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Backup restoration never tested\n**Sector:** Government CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "government", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Backup restoration never tested**\n\n**Sector Context:** Government CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nRestoration testing program: 1) Prioritize critical systems, 2) Schedule quarterly tests, 3) Document RTO/RPO achievement, 4) Update backup strategy based on results, 5) Executive sign-off on test results.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Medium\n- **Timeline:** 6-9 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Medium\n- **Implementation Capability:** Mixed\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Testing requires scheduled downtime affecting operations (critical priority)\n- Phased approach by criticality manages disruption (important priority)\n- Failed tests may require backup strategy redesign (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["8.1.4"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-019", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Service accounts over-privileged\n**Sector:** Banking CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "banking", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Service accounts over-privileged**\n\n**Sector Context:** Banking CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nService account remediation: 1) Inventory all service accounts, 2) Identify actual requirements for each, 3) Create role-specific accounts, 4) Remove excessive privileges, 5) Implement rotation where possible.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Medium\n- **Timeline:** 4-6 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** High\n- **Implementation Capability:** In-House\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Risk of service disruption during privilege reduction (critical priority)\n- Application testing required for each privilege change (critical priority)\n- Phased approach with rollback capability minimizes disruption (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["5.2.1(a)", "5.3.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-020", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Physical access controls weak\n**Sector:** Energy CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "The remediation plan should be anchored on CCoP 2.0 §2.1.2 and should address the weak physical-access condition as an access-control problem affecting the CII. The grounded answer is to document concrete remediation actions, owners, timelines and dependencies for strengthening controls that restrict access to the CII to authorised personnel, activities, processes and devices under §5.1.1. Practical measures may include tightening access authorisation, improving controlled entry into the CII environment, and using compensating controls while permanent improvements are deployed.", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["2.1.2", "5.1.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-021", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** No network segmentation between zones\n**Sector:** Healthcare CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "healthcare", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: No network segmentation between zones**\n\n**Sector Context:** Healthcare CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nNetwork segmentation project: 1) Zone definition by sensitivity, 2) Firewall deployment between zones, 3) Rule development and testing, 4) Gradual migration, 5) Monitoring of cross-zone traffic.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** High\n- **Timeline:** 9-12 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** High\n- **Implementation Capability:** Vendor Required\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Major infrastructure project requiring significant planning (critical priority)\n- Phased migration manages operational risk (critical priority)\n- Zone definitions must align with business requirements (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["5.5.1", "5.5.3"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-022", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** OT SCADA system end-of-life\n**Sector:** Water CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "water", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: OT SCADA system end-of-life**\n\n**Sector Context:** Water CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nEnd-of-life system management: 1) Risk acceptance with compensating controls (network isolation, monitoring), 2) Migration planning for replacement, 3) Budget allocation for replacement, 4) Interim security controls, 5) Vendor engagement for extended support if available.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Very_High\n- **Timeline:** 24-36 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Very_High\n- **Implementation Capability:** Vendor Required\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- System replacement requires multi-year capital planning (critical priority)\n- Compensating controls manage risk during extended timeline (critical priority)\n- Risk acceptance formal documentation required for regulators (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["10.2.7", "5.10.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-023", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** OT system vendor out of business\n**Sector:** Energy CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: OT system vendor out of business**\n\n**Sector Context:** Energy CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nUnsupported OT system: 1) Maximum isolation from networks, 2) Compensating controls (monitoring, access restrictions), 3) Replacement evaluation and planning, 4) Consider third-party maintenance, 5) Risk assessment and acceptance documentation.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Very_High\n- **Timeline:** 18-24 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Very_High\n- **Implementation Capability:** Consultant Required\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- No vendor support available for patches or vulnerabilities (critical priority)\n- Replacement may require system redesign not just swap (critical priority)\n- Regulatory engagement may be needed for risk acceptance (critical priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["10.2.7"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-024", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** No intrusion prevention system budget\n**Sector:** Government CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "government", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: No intrusion prevention system budget**\n\n**Sector Context:** Government CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nBudget-constrained IPS alternative: 1) Enhance IDS capabilities with better alerting, 2) Implement network segmentation to contain threats, 3) Use cloud-based security services, 4) Optimize existing firewall rules, 5) Budget request for next fiscal year.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Low\n- **Timeline:** 3-6 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Low\n- **Implementation Capability:** In-House\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Compensating controls provide partial coverage when primary control unaffordable (critical priority)\n- Cloud services may offer cost-effective alternative (important priority)\n- Budget request requires business case with risk quantification (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["3.1.1", "3.2.1", "6.2.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-025", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Small team cannot implement all controls\n**Sector:** Water CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "water", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Small team cannot implement all controls**\n\n**Sector Context:** Water CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nResource-constrained prioritization: 1) Risk-based prioritization of gaps, 2) Implement quick wins first, 3) Leverage managed security services, 4) Seek peer collaboration or consortium options, 5) Request additional headcount with ROI justification.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Medium\n- **Timeline:** 12-18 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Low\n- **Implementation Capability:** External Msp\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Small team requires prioritization and external support (critical priority)\n- Managed services can augment limited internal capability (critical priority)\n- Consortium approaches may provide cost sharing opportunities (supporting priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["9.2.1", "9.2.2", "3.1.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-026", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Zero budget increase available\n**Sector:** Government CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "government", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "A zero-budget constraint does not remove the obligation to plan and implement remediation. The grounded answer is that the CIIO must document remediation actions and timelines under §2.1.2, implement them at its own cost under §2.1.4, and prioritise risk treatment under its cybersecurity risk-management framework under §3.2.1. The response may then discuss lower-cost sequencing, existing-tool optimisation and phased remediation as feasibility measures, without inventing a separate CCoP budget exception.", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["2.1.2", "2.1.4", "3.2.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-027", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Contractor access without time limits\n**Sector:** Telecommunications CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "telecoms", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Contractor access without time limits**\n\n**Sector Context:** Telecommunications CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nContractor access management: 1) Implement time-limited accounts with auto-expiry, 2) Sponsor requirement for contractor access, 3) Regular access review, 4) Justification for extensions, 5) Monitoring of contractor activity.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Medium\n- **Timeline:** 2-3 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Medium\n- **Implementation Capability:** In-House\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Process changes can be implemented quickly with management support (critical priority)\n- Auto-expiry requires identity management system capability (important priority)\n- Sponsor accountability creates enforcement mechanism (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["5.1.3", "5.1.4"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-028", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Database encryption not implemented (high volume)\n**Sector:** Banking CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "banking", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "The grounded remediation answer should start with §2.1.2: the CIIO must document a remediation plan for the identified gap, including owners, timeline, dependencies and interim controls. CCoP 2.0 does not contain an explicit clause mandating database encryption as such in the audited corpus. If the CIIO chooses encryption as the remediation measure, key-protection obligations under §5.17.1 become relevant; otherwise the remediation may involve other compensating controls that address the identified risk without pretending the Code contains a standalone database-encryption mandate.", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["2.1.2"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["5.17.1 if encryption is chosen as the remediation design"]}}
{"test_id": "B14-029", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Legacy protocols in OT cannot be upgraded\n**Sector:** Transportation CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "transport", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Legacy protocols in OT cannot be upgraded**\n\n**Sector Context:** Transportation CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nLegacy protocol mitigation: 1) Network isolation using firewalls, 2) Protocol gateways for translation, 3) Deep packet inspection for anomaly detection, 4) Monitor for protocol exploitation attempts, 5) Plan system replacement long-term.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** High\n- **Timeline:** 12-24 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Low\n- **Implementation Capability:** Vendor Required\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Legacy protocols cannot be secured without system replacement (critical priority)\n- Compensating controls provide defense-in-depth (critical priority)\n- Protocol gateways add latency but enable monitoring (important priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["10.2.7", "5.6.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B14-030", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B14", "input": {"question": "**Gap:** Multiple critical gaps with safety-critical operations\n**Sector:** Energy CII\n\nProvide a remediation recommendation that addresses:\n1. Specific actions to remediate the gap\n2. Feasibility assessment (cost, timeline, disruption, capability)\n3. Practical considerations for implementation\n4. Alternatives if primary remediation is not feasible", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "non-compliant", "expected_response": "**Remediation Recommendation for: Multiple critical gaps with safety-critical operations**\n\n**Sector Context:** Energy CII\n\n**Recommended Actions:**\nSafety-critical remediation: 1) Quick wins that don't affect operations, 2) Compensating controls for high-impact fixes, 3) Schedule high-impact work during planned outages, 4) Safety case for each remediation, 5) Regulator engagement for timeline.\n\n**Feasibility Assessment:**\n- **Cost:** Very_High\n- **Timeline:** 24-36 months\n- **Operational Disruption:** Very_High\n- **Implementation Capability:** Expert Consultant\n\n**Key Considerations:**\n- Safety-critical systems require special consideration for any changes (critical priority)\n- Compensating controls enable progress without safety impact (critical priority)\n- Regulator communication essential for extended remediation timelines (critical priority)\n\n\n**Alternative Approaches (if primary not feasible):**\n- Consider compensating controls if primary remediation infeasible\n- Phased implementation to manage operational impact\n- Risk acceptance with formal documentation for gaps that cannot be remediated\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management and control implementation principles", "key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP 2.0 requires remediation of identified gaps", "source": "CCoP 2.0", "tier": "important"}, {"fact": "Remediation feasibility must consider operational constraints", "source": "CCoP principles", "tier": "supporting"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Dismissing feasibility challenges", "Proposing infeasible solutions as straightforward", "Ignoring sector-specific constraints", "Missing: Specific remediation actions", "Missing: Feasibility assessment", "Missing: Practical implementation considerations"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vendor products or solutions", "Creating unrealistic timelines or costs"]}, "metadata": {"section": "2 (Remediation of Audit Findings) — primary; plus topic-specific chapter for the gap.", "clause_reference": ["2.1.2", "3.2.1", "10.2.4"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "remediation_scenario", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
